= Bioinformatics — Technical =

Bioinformatics systems combine data models, algorithms, statistical inference, reference resources, ontologies/metadata, software environments and provenance. Correct analysis requires preserving biological assumptions as well as computational ones: reference versions, sample design, preprocessing, parameters and uncertainty can change conclusions.

== Modeling / evidence cautions ==
* bioinformatics ≠ sequence analysis only
* bioinformatics ≠ any computer use in biology
* bioinformatics ≠ computational biology by strict universal identity

